{
  "id": 512941687,
  "iid": 25977,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "lbmc: display TSNI Request in Info column for RXREQ packets",
  "description": "The UME ranged retransmission request work for UM 6.17 is already in master. This adds one further refinement to UME_RXREQ handling: when the RXREQ header's TSNI Request flag (0x4000) is set, the packet is being used to request Topic Sequence Number Information rather than performing a traditional retransmission request.\n\nThe Info column now displays RXREQ (TSNI Request) instead of plain RXREQ in that case, to make this dual usage visible at a glance without having to open the packet details.\n\nImplementation\n\n- dissect_nhdr_ume_rxreq() now takes an output parameter reporting whether the TSNI flag is set\n- lbmc_determine_msg_type() accepts that flag and returns the TSNI-specific string when set\n- Main dissection loop tracks the flag via a new rxreq_is_tsni variable\n\nTesting\n\n- Test capture tsni_req.pcapng included\n- Verified via tshark: TSNI-flagged RXREQ shows RXREQ (TSNI Request); plain RXREQ packets (checked against ranged_rx.pcapng, 37 packets) are unaffected\n- Builds clean, no compiler warnings\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 noreply@anthropic.com",
  "state": "merged",
