      "title": "lbmc: add UME ranged retransmission request dissection for UM 6.17",
      "message": "lbmc: add UME ranged retransmission request dissection for UM 6.17\n\nAdded dissection support for LBMC_NHDR_UME_RANGED_RXREQ (0x1F)\nintroduced in Ultra Messaging 6.17.\n\nThis message type allows receivers to request a range of sequence\nnumbers in a single retransmission request, used for late-join and\noff-transport recovery scenarios. More efficient than issuing\nindividual retransmission requests for each lost message.\n\nStructure dissected (12 bytes):\n- next_hdr, hdr_len, flags (ignore bit)\n- first_seqnum - start of requested sequence range\n- last_seqnum - end of requested sequence range\n\nDisplay filters:\n- lbmc.ume_ranged_rxreq\n- lbmc.ume_ranged_rxreq.first_seqnum\n- lbmc.ume_ranged_rxreq.last_seqnum\n\nRelated capability flag (already present in dissector):\n- lbmc.ume_capability.flags.ranged_rx_flag (0x1000)\n\nAlso modified the Info column to display \"RXREQ (TSNI Request)\"\ninstead of just \"RXREQ\" when the UME_RXREQ header has the TSNI\nRequest flag (0x4000) set.\n\nWhen this flag is set, the RXREQ packet is being used to request Topic\nSequence Number Information rather than a traditional retransmission\nrequest. The Info column text clarifies this dual usage while\nmaintaining clarity about the underlying packet structure.\n\nImplementation:\n- Modified dissect_nhdr_ume_rxreq() to check TSNI flag and report via\n  output parameter\n- Updated lbmc_determine_msg_type() to handle TSNI-flagged RXREQ\n- Added rxreq_is_tsni tracking variable in main dissection loop\n\nTest capture tsni_req.pcapng validates the Info column display.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n",
      "author_name": "Sherwin Clutter",
